prompt:
A real photograph of the yard of a small family farm in Brandenburg on a sunny morning in early autumn, taken as a visitor standing by the gate a few metres away would take it with a good phone camera, in a tall vertical picture, everything in sharp focus. Natural colours, warm morning sunlight from the right. The textures of real weathered wood, straw, feathers, fur, mud, stone, metal, grass, fabric and skin.

The first reference picture shows the young woman in three-quarter view, the second from the front: her face, her dark blonde hair tied back in a ponytail, her build and her height stay exactly as in them. Use them for the person only; her clothes here are a red-and-black checked shirt open over a white T-shirt, blue jeans and dark-green rubber boots.

Every object and every animal stands on its own, with a little space around it, so that the eye can tell at once where each thing is. Nothing in the picture carries any writing, numbers or print: the crates and buckets are plain, the sacks are plain brown cloth, the apples have plain unmarked skins with no stickers, and nothing carries a sign, a logo or a brand.

THE FRONT of the picture, the lower part, the packed earth of the yard with a few puddles:
- a wicker basket full of brown eggs standing on the ground;
- three brown hens pecking at the ground around the basket;
- a grey metal milk pail standing on the ground, with a wooden crate full of red apples with plain unmarked skins next to it;
- a black-and-white sheepdog lying on the ground on the right, its head up, watching the hens.

THE YOUNG WOMAN of the reference pictures stands in the middle of the yard, seen whole from her head to her rubber boots, which stand on the earth with their shadow beside them. She is caught in the middle of feeding the horse: she holds a red apple with a plain unmarked skin out on her flat open hand towards a brown horse that stretches its head over a wooden fence on the left, and she laughs; her other hand holds a second red apple against her chest.

THE MIDDLE of the picture:
- on the left, the brown horse behind the wooden fence, its head stretched towards the apple;
- behind the fence, a black-and-white cow standing in a green meadow with a few white flowers;
- a pink pig standing in a small muddy pen with a low wooden fence, on the right;
- a farmer, a man of about sixty with a grey beard, a flat cap and a blue checked shirt, carrying a bale of straw past the pig pen, smiling;
- a small boy of about six in a straw hat and a blue T-shirt, crouching, holding out grain to a hen;
- a stone well with a little wooden roof and a bucket hanging on a rope;
- a wooden bench against the wall of the house.

THE BACK of the picture:
- on the right, the farmhouse, an old brick house with a red tiled roof, white windows with green shutters and a green front door;
- on the left, a wooden barn with a big open door, a wooden ladder leaning against its wall, a stack of chopped firewood beside it, two orange pumpkins and a plain brown sack standing by the door;
- a cat sitting on the low stone wall between the house and the barn;
- a bird sitting on the ridge of the roof;
- a big apple tree with red apples next to the barn;
- further back, a gentle green hill with a few white sheep, a wheat field, a dark forest on the horizon and a blue sky with a few white clouds and the sun.
